# Benchmark run artifacts.
#
# runs/ is ~750 MB and most of it is raw logs and screenshots. The analysis
# files -- reports.txt and summary.txt -- ARE kept, because every number in the
# documentation is derived from them and a repository where the claims cannot
# be re-derived is worth much less.
#
# The rest is excluded for two reasons. Size: 533 MB of PNGs, an 11 MB
# proton.log, a 45 MB CSV. And privacy: the Steam and Proton logs carry the
# author's Linux username in ~2250 absolute paths, a private LAN address, and
# in three game.log files a persistent telemetry client ID that the publisher
# could correlate to an account. None of that is needed to reproduce anything.
runs/**/*.png
runs/**/proton.log
runs/**/steam-stdout.txt
runs/**/harness.log
runs/**/clean.log
runs/**/game.log
runs/**/threads.txt
runs/**/*.qpa
runs/*.csv
runs/**/samples.csv
runs/**/marks.csv
runs/**/guest-raw.csv

# Local investigation notes and captured logs from the bring-up. Same problem
# as above: usernames and a telemetry client ID, no reproduction value.
evidence/

# Build output. Every one of these has its source next to it.
tests/*.spv
tests/bigconst
tests/coherence
tests/cstest
tests/disptest
tests/drawcost
tests/drirctest
tests/gfxtest
tests/memtest
tests/occtest
tests/preambletest
tests/robtest
tests/ssboload
tests/ssboload2
tests/statetest
tests/tstest
tests/waittest

# Prebuilt x86-64 FEX guest thunks. Redistributing third-party binaries raises
# a licensing question this repository should not answer; build them from FEX.
fex/GuestThunks/*.so

# Backups and scratch.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.backup-*

# Packaging output. Both are rebuilt from mesa-source.env and the spec; neither
# is worth 40 MB of git history.
out/
packaging/srpm/
